WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.140
The day is Jan 5th, 2012.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:08.650
At an undisclosed offsite location, Dr. Bannon
leaves home and begins his commute to work.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.790
While in the car he plays a video on his phone
of his 12 year old’s birthday party from

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.190
the previous night.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.160
The sight of it makes him smile.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.699
He would need that smile he thought, as today
was not like any other.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:21.949
Today was different.

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:26.739
He had been anxious about the coming day for
several weeks now, ever since the near-unanimous

00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:32.940
vote by the O5 Council that the containment
chamber of SCP-106 was to be re-opened.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.000
The opportunity was “too great to be wasted”
they said.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.890
The research that could be gained too tempting..

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:46.079
Studying SCP-106’s molecular makeup, it’s
unique ability to open a “pocket dimension”,

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:50.219
or even just the black sludge-like substance
that appeared whenever the subject traveled

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:55.320
through solid objects, was far too valuable
to science to be outweighed by its potential

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.480
for danger.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.949
He pleaded with them.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:00:59.350
Begged them.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.170
But as Dr. Bannon and his team of 7 researchers
and accompaniment of 40 security personnel

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.390
began applying their protective equipment,
he couldn’t help but think that he could

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.660
have done more to stop this.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:14.300
Only God knew how hard he had tried to make
them see reason.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.540
He had seen what had happened in previous
containment breaches at the facility.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.610
He had seen what it’d done to the poor members
of SCP staff that became it’s victims.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.120
Fates worse than death.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.030
Limbs.. a mangled mess of melted fused skin.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:32.450
Faces sunken and hollow with eyes and tongues
burned out.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.700
He shuddered to think of what would happen
if containment failed again this time.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.310
But to spite his misgivings, he knew full
well that regardless of his participation,

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.060
this research mission would go on with or
without him.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:50.060
And no one knew as much about containing SCP-106
than he did.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.810
Slowly, they proceeded to dismantle each of
the containment facilities' outer barriers.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:02:01.710
16 separate circular chambers surrounded SCP-106’s
inner containment facility, each filled with

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.990
a variety of different fluids.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:09.350
Fluids in each chamber varied in consistency
and viscosity from ionized water to ammonia

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.890
to kerosene.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:16.200
SCP-106 had the peculiar ability to be able
to change its molecular makeup to meld with

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.500
objects and phase through solid forms like
walls and doors.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.480
It could literally melt into the space between
walls.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:28.620
This made containing SCP-106 almost impossible
by conventional methods.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.740
Liquids confused the creature enough to slow
him down.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.310
In theory anyways.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:37.180
The secondary containment chambers were a
recent addition to the facility since the

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.280
breach incident 3 years ago.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.700
Dr. Bannon had been a new addition to the
research staff then.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:48.280
He had joined the team with bright eyes and
a desire to use their research to help society.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.569
Little did he know he would instead do everything
in his power to keep whatever they found from

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:54.660
ever leaving the facility.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:00.490
Back then a breach in the containment of SCP-106
led to countless deaths of SCP personnel when

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.940
a researcher working on the top floor of the
outer layer of the containment facility, unknowing

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.630
of the danger they were in, brought his child
to work one day.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:13.040
It was thought the outer layers of the facility
were enough to be considered a safe zone from

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.440
the inner vault that was SCP-106’s containment.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.290
But it wasn’t enough to stop the Old Man.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:25.770
SCP-106 preferred human prey between the ages
of 10 and 25.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:31.320
And the sound of a child’s cry or yell was
enough to capture it’s immediate attention.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.430
What proceeded was unimaginable horror.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:38.860
But to spite the unfortunate events of the
previous breach, the expedition continued

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.030
their dissent into the bowels of the building.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.690
After several hours of draining individual
fluid chambers one by one and inputting complex

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:51.790
codes and biometric scans from simultaneous
top security clearance personnel at a time,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:57.830
the expedition team had eventually reached
the lower levels of SCP-106’s containment

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:58.850
facility.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:05.180
Suspended in midair by ELO IID electromagnetic
supports, in the center of a vast subterranean

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:11.489
chamber, was a massive lead-lined steel cube,
40 layers thick, each layer separated by 36

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:18.389
cm of empty space, with support struts between
layers randomly spaced to confuse SCP-106

00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:21.630
from being able to phase through one layer
to the next.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:25.900
Surrounding the cube on every surface were
military grade automated light systems capable

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:31.750
of 80,000 lumens apiece, spaced every two
feet around the perimeter of the inner containment

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.750
chamber.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.569
The team felt their resolve chip away the
closer they got to the suspended structure.

00:04:36.569 --> 00:04:41.080
Dr. Bannon motioned to overhead surveillance
cameras above the cube and waited.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.740
Slowly, the cube was lowered to the ground
until it hit the floor with a soft thud that

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.439
lightly rumbled the ground under the expedition
team’s feet.

00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:53.909
With a resentful look up at the red dot on
the camera above, Dr. Bannon initiated the

00:04:53.909 --> 00:04:55.479
Release Protocol.

00:04:55.479 --> 00:05:00.110
All seven researchers input their key cards
and submitted themselves to retina scans as

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:04.979
the 40 security personnel established defensive
positions on every side of the lead-lined

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:05.979
cube.

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:08.819
For a moment, everyone held their breath in
silence.

00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:13.550
You could almost feel the thumping of everyone’s
nervous heartbeats as they looked on to Dr.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.529
Bannon as he pulled out his key card.

00:05:16.529 --> 00:05:21.030
Everyone knew that as soon as it was scanned,
the barrier between them and The Old Man would

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.379
no longer exist.

00:05:22.379 --> 00:05:26.800
If the rest of the personnel could see Bannon’s
hand shaking as he gripped the key card tightly

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.630
between his fingers, it would cause a possible
mass panic among the whole team.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:35.749
As the spear-heading researcher on the job
that day, Bannon knew what he was up against

00:05:35.749 --> 00:05:38.830
just the same as every one else, if not more.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.439
He knew he couldn’t show the fear that was
pulsing through his veins.

00:05:42.439 --> 00:05:44.749
This wasn’t his first rodeo here at the
Foundation.

00:05:44.749 --> 00:05:49.580
He took a moment to collect his thoughts:
“Get ahold of yourself Bannon” He thought.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:53.070
Dr. Bannon took a deep breath and scanned
the card.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.199
The door slowly opened.

00:05:55.199 --> 00:05:59.270
Armed with powerful rifle-length flashlights,
the researchers cautiously waded into the

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:02.060
dark entrance of the large cube.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:05.580
Inside the structure they found a cell with
a solid steel door.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:10.349
Signs of corrosion could be seen on the door’s
handle and the outer walls of the cell, rust

00:06:10.349 --> 00:06:14.110
and rotted iron, but no breaches in the integrity
of the cell.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:16.729
There were no more security codes at this
door.

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:19.689
It was a simple round metal turn lock.

00:06:19.689 --> 00:06:23.559
Dr. Bannon swallowed, and began to turn the
handle open.

00:06:23.559 --> 00:06:27.229
The sound of metal on metal echoed through
the chamber as the door creaked open, each

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:30.389
of the researchers immediately pointing their
flashlights into the room.

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:37.139
There in the corner, standing motionless and
undisturbed, stood SCP-106.

00:06:37.139 --> 00:06:38.139
The Old Man.

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:42.070
He stood with eyes closed, locked in a dormant
state.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.279
The researchers had planned for this.

00:06:44.279 --> 00:06:49.990
SCP-106 spent up to 3 months at a time in
this subdued state in between periods of otherwise

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:54.919
“agitation”, where it would lash out at
it’s containment and attempt breach.

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:57.159
The research team wasted no time.

00:06:57.159 --> 00:07:01.849
They began to collect data on the creature’s
biological makeup, taking whatever samples

00:07:01.849 --> 00:07:06.569
they could from the walls and floors, and
recording photo and video of the specimen

00:07:06.569 --> 00:07:10.869
while collecting any method of conventional
analysis they could manage under the given

00:07:10.869 --> 00:07:11.869
circumstances.

00:07:11.869 --> 00:07:17.169
Dr. Bannon kept an eye on the old man’s
face the entire time, refusing to look away

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:21.819
for one second for fear of it waking in the
absence of his gaze.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:27.379
But to his relief, the creature did not stir,
and the data collection process went smoothly.

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:31.289
In a short period of time the team had packed
their gear and had proceeded to carefully

00:07:31.289 --> 00:07:35.479
retreat from the inner chamber of the cube,
making sure to keep their lights pointed at

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:37.590
the creature the entire time.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:41.551
Once the team exited the steel lined cube
they motioned again to the camera and the

00:07:41.551 --> 00:07:45.419
huge heavy doors of the cube closed back in
on itself.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:50.801
The electromagnetic supports came back online
and the cube was suspended once again in 3-dimensional

00:07:50.801 --> 00:07:54.969
space without any immediate contact with solid
surfaces.

00:07:54.969 --> 00:07:59.330
The security detail began packing up their
positions as everyone seemed to take a collective

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.740
sigh of relief.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:03.940
That's when Dr. Bannon noticed the security
camera.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:06.529
The red dot on the device had stopped blinking.

00:08:06.529 --> 00:08:08.099
The camera was off.

00:08:08.099 --> 00:08:12.440
A sudden feeling of dread entered Dr. Bannon’s
stomach as he turned in time to see all the

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.960
cameras around the room turning off.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:19.759
Before he could react the chamber was plunged
into darkness as the electricity left the

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:20.759
room.

00:08:20.759 --> 00:08:25.110
In the immediate darkness came a deafening
bang followed by a gust of wind and the weight

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:30.340
of a force strong enough to shake the ground
and knock the researchers off their feet.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.800
The power to the electromagnetic supports
were down.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.680
The cube had fallen.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.029
Dr. Bannon shouted to his team to immediately
exit the facility.

00:08:39.029 --> 00:08:41.909
He reached for his flashlight in the darkness.

00:08:41.909 --> 00:08:44.800
He could hear screams in the background, gunfire.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:49.630
He managed to illuminate the space in front
of him and saw his molecular biologist Dr.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.560
Berns scrambling to get her gear back up over
her shoulder.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.500
“Leave it!”, Dr. Bannon cried, only to
see a hand emerge from beneath her and pull

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:03.130
her down into a black viscous substance that
swallowed her whole and then vanished into

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:04.940
solid concrete.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:09.670
After hearing the cries to his left he swung
his flashlight just in time to see him.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:14.980
The old man had it’s hand on the chest of
a security personnel and entered him, exiting

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:18.920
through the other side leaving a gaping hole
in between.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:24.829
Bullets were useless, as they seemed to get
trapped on entry of his body, slowly melting

00:09:24.829 --> 00:09:26.550
into his skin.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:32.500
SCP-106 then vanished into the floor and appeared
behind another member of the security detail,

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.810
grabbing him by the heel and dragging him
as he pleaded and reached out to Dr. Bannon

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:41.940
for help, pulling him halfway into the wall
and then letting go as the creature melted

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:47.060
into the space between the walls, leaving
behind half the poor man’s body bleeding

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.620
and still squirming to get away.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:55.220
One by one he could hear his researchers crying
out for help before their voices were extinguished.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:59.440
Before he could think of what to do next,
the power came back on, and light flooded

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:01.180
into the large room.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:06.050
He gazed at the creature as it stood momentarily
stunned by the influx of light.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:11.649
The old man had gaunt piercing hollow eyes
in a face covered in dark melting skin and

00:10:11.649 --> 00:10:15.089
a lipless mouth that displayed terrible decaying
teeth.

00:10:15.089 --> 00:10:20.750
It’s corrosive hand had a grasp on the arm
of Dr. Bryer, the physicist, burning the skin

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:24.209
beneath it’s grip as he cried out in pain.

00:10:24.209 --> 00:10:30.470
And then, without warning, the creature placed
a hand on the wall of the metal cube and disappeared

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:35.740
into it, pulling the doctor in with him…
into the pocket dimension between the walls.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:42.470
48 hrs later, in containment site 19, located
in the state of [data expunged], SCP personnel

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.300
open the door to an observation chamber where
SCP-049

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:49.660
is led in wearing steel covered hand restraints.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:54.910
On the other side of a glass panel, Dr. Blake
sat impatiently, watching the humanoid creature

00:10:54.910 --> 00:11:00.089
known as SCP-049, the “Plague Doctor”,
take a seat and face his direction.

00:11:00.089 --> 00:11:04.070
Dr. Blake hesitated to address the entity
that sat in front of him.

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:07.949
But putting aside his reservations, he spoke
into the microphone.

00:11:07.949 --> 00:11:14.350
Blake informed SCP-049 of the recent breach
that had transpired at the SCP-106 containment

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:15.350
site.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.529
The doctor seemed intrigued at the news.

00:11:17.529 --> 00:11:21.199
And when asked if he would provide assistance,
the doctor agreed.

00:11:21.199 --> 00:11:28.160
SCP-049 had exhibited abilities to produce
instances of SCP-049-2, reanimated corpses

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.259
that he alone had the ability to control by
will.

00:11:31.259 --> 00:11:36.269
In the past the Plague Doctor had been allowed
certain..privileges..deceased subjects for

00:11:36.269 --> 00:11:41.779
the doctor to experiment on in his quest to
find a cure for what he referred to as “the

00:11:41.779 --> 00:11:45.879
Pestilence”, though none of the researchers
could pinpoint exactly what the symptoms of

00:11:45.879 --> 00:11:50.069
this perceived illness was or any specifics
about it at all.

00:11:50.069 --> 00:11:55.750
However the supply of subjects was halted
after an incident where SCP-049 struck a personnel

00:11:55.750 --> 00:12:00.820
member, killing him instantly with his “touch
of death”, an ability that ceases all bodily

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.100
function upon contact.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:07.519
Since then the Plague Doctor refused to cooperate
unless he was provided with live subjects

00:12:07.519 --> 00:12:08.600
for experimentation.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:11.149
Up to this point, he had been denied.

00:12:11.149 --> 00:12:14.379
But Dr. Blake needed the Plague Doctor’s
help.

00:12:14.379 --> 00:12:16.990
And time was not on his side.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:24.279
Dr. Blake agreed to provide SCP-049 with several
live D-Class personnel in return for his assistance.

00:12:24.279 --> 00:12:28.629
As we’ve come to learn time and time again
here on SCP Explained, the Foundation has

00:12:28.629 --> 00:12:32.610
no qualms about ridding the lives of these
ex-death row inmates.

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:37.220
D-Class are essentially the Foundation’s
lab rats and treating them as such is more

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:41.879
than worth it if dealing with an SCP-106 containment
breach.

00:12:41.879 --> 00:12:44.420
Bring in the orange jumpsuits!

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:45.589
“Splendid!”

00:12:45.589 --> 00:12:47.189
remarked 049.

00:12:47.189 --> 00:12:52.610
The Plague Doctor was taken to the secret
site of SCP-106’s containment facility and

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:57.520
briefed on The Old Man’s ability to meld
and travel between walls, floors, and solid

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:58.520
surfaces.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:02.970
As well as its ability to pull objects into
its own pocket dimension, of which there was

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.970
little information about.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:09.939
SCP-049 grew more and more intrigued by the
description of the old man.

00:13:09.939 --> 00:13:14.550
Upon arriving, a laboratory was prepared at
the site for SCP-049.

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:20.439
For proxies to serve as lures to bait SCP-106,
the team procured the bodies of a recent public

00:13:20.439 --> 00:13:24.760
transportation bus wreckage that had left
12 younger adults dead.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:29.399
As the Plague Doctor began his surgeries on
them, Doctor Bannon could think only of the

00:13:29.399 --> 00:13:31.060
prior containment breach.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.899
The staff suffered many casualties to personnel.

00:13:33.899 --> 00:13:39.110
And ever since then anyone under the age of
30 were banned entry within 20 miles of the

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.720
containment site.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:44.910
Just as Doctor Bannon began to rub his temple
thinking about how they managed to return

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:49.360
SCP-106 to his cell that day, there was yell
of excitement:

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.519
“Marvelous!”

00:13:50.519 --> 00:13:52.730
cried out SCP-049.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.149
The Plague Doctor informed SCP staff that
he had finished his work and the surgeries

00:13:57.149 --> 00:13:59.620
had been of paramount success.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:04.819
The doctor had indeed produced 12 instances
of SCP-049-2 as predicted.

00:14:04.819 --> 00:14:07.490
The subjects were horrid abominations.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:12.279
Some with inverted faces and others with added
appendages and gaping holes where limbs should

00:14:12.279 --> 00:14:13.279
be.

00:14:13.279 --> 00:14:14.439
But they were ambient.

00:14:14.439 --> 00:14:20.389
And the research staff would soon learn if
they would be enough to lure SCP-106 back

00:14:20.389 --> 00:14:21.829
into containment.

00:14:21.829 --> 00:14:26.440
Staring at the dimly lit white room crowded
with malformed ambient corpses, Dr. Bannon

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.819
couldn’t help but feel a sense of dread
fill the pit of his stomach.

00:14:29.819 --> 00:14:32.220
But there was no time to second guess.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:37.940
With rifles and flashlights in hand the team
led the troop of SCP-049-2s out and down the

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:43.249
concrete hallways and into a large freight
elevator that led down to the vast chamber

00:14:43.249 --> 00:14:48.760
that housed the inner containment cube that
was SCP-106’s home since arriving at the

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:49.810
facility.

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:53.050
The drone-like -2s did not speak during this
trip.

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.220
They did not blink.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:58.949
They simply stared straight ahead and acted
at the behest of the Plague Doctor without

00:14:58.949 --> 00:15:00.410
any verbal input.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:05.089
The macabre parade arrived at the entrance
of the cube and proceeded inside.

00:15:05.089 --> 00:15:12.069
Dr, Bannon informed SCP-049 that the -2s needed
to make noises of some kind, to cry out if

00:15:12.069 --> 00:15:13.069
they could.

00:15:13.069 --> 00:15:16.620
Anything would work, as long as it was audible
enough.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.300
The Plague Doctor nodded his head.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:23.769
And all 12 of the reanimated corpses began
to scream in terrifying unison.

00:15:23.769 --> 00:15:27.999
In the hollow distance, a roar was heard in
response.

00:15:27.999 --> 00:15:29.930
It dripped from the ceiling.

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:34.899
First a drop, then many more until a puddle
formed on the ground in front of the cube,

00:15:34.899 --> 00:15:37.379
the Plague Doctor approaching with intrigue.

00:15:37.379 --> 00:15:43.670
Out of the floor rose up the creature known
as SCP-106, coming face to face with the Plague

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:44.829
Doctor.

00:15:44.829 --> 00:15:48.339
Upon seeing the creature, SCP-049 was ecstatic.

00:15:48.339 --> 00:15:53.230
He began to examine SCP-106 closely without
fear of bodily harm.

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:57.879
With lightning speed he produced a vial and
pincers from a medicine bag of black leather

00:15:57.879 --> 00:16:03.129
he kept under his robes and snatched a sample
of the creature’s black viscous skin.

00:16:03.129 --> 00:16:07.750
The Plague Doctor was overjoyed:
“This will lead to my greatest work, and

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.720
the cure for the Pestilence once and for all!”

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:17.399
But the old man did not seem to acknowledge
or enjoy the presence of SCP-049 and reacted

00:16:17.399 --> 00:16:20.950
violently, lashing out to strike the Plague
Doctor.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:26.939
Sensing danger, 049 jumped back and willed
the 049-2s to attack the creature.

00:16:26.939 --> 00:16:32.680
But before they could reach it, SCP-106 melted
into a pool of black and disappeared into

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:33.740
the floor.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:36.269
The instances looked around dazed.

00:16:36.269 --> 00:16:40.430
Another black pool appeared under one of them,
causing it to fall into the portal and then

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:44.500
fall out from the ceiling elsewhere in the
vast stadium-sized room.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:49.970
Another pool opened under one of the ambient
thralls, sucking it down into the black abyss.

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:51.379
And then another.

00:16:51.379 --> 00:16:52.420
And another.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:56.860
And soon loud thuds could be heard echoing
through the chamber as bodies began to appear

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:02.310
from the top of the hundred foot ceiling,
falling to a splatter on the concrete floor

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:03.310
below.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:09.940
Upon witnessing SCP-106’s abilities first
hand, SCP-049 nodded to Dr. Bannon as he swiftly

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:16.010
packed up his medicine bag and made for the
door, only to be blocked by SCP-106’s materializing

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.040
form.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:21.020
The Plague Doctor grew angry and struck the
neck of the old man with his cold touch of

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.020
death.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.880
But it seemed to have no effect on SCP-106.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:30.710
The black substance on his body started to
creep up over 049’s hand, sizzling and searing

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:34.360
skin and flesh as it went up the forearm.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:39.560
Sensing danger, the Plague Doctor pulled out
a large scalpel and in one quick motion sliced

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:41.750
off his own arm at the elbow.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:46.310
The severed limb fell to the floor, engulfed
by the black bubbling substance.

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:51.220
SCP-106 then lunged at the Doctor who’s
quick agility allowed him to dodge and make

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:52.560
for the doorway.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:57.990
Once in the hall SCP-049 quickly pulled out
a roll of brown gauze from his medical bag

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:02.910
and began to wrap his bleeding wound tight
as he hurried through the dimly lit corridor,

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.140
lights flickering on and off.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:10.180
As SCP-049 turned a corner a black substance
appeared on the wall in front of him and a

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:12.940
chair came flying out of it towards his head.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:17.680
The Doctor dodged it but did not dodge a sharp
metal spike that materialized from another

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:20.230
hole appearing on the wall to his left.

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:24.290
It pierced the outside of his knee, causing
his movement to be slowed.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:28.870
Hearing the sound of clanking metal, the doctor
looked up in time to see a desk falling out

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.300
of another dimensional portal above him.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:38.380
He managed to roll sideways, missing the blow,
but straight into another of SCP-106’s portals,

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:42.440
causing the doctor to fall through the wall
and into the floor of the room below.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:47.380
With a falling crash the doctor landed in
the lower room and looked around quickly seeking

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.160
to regain his footing.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:54.670
The old man was nowhere to be seen, but he
could hear him, bumping in the darkness, traveling

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:56.440
through the walls of the building.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:19:00.060
The Plague Doctor quickly analyzed the office
room for something useful.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.940
On the wall he found a map of the facility
and studied the schematics.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.520
On the floor was a dead body.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:10.090
He crouched down close to it and stabbed it
with a syringe from his cloak, animating the

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:16.220
corpse and commanding it to run, serving as
a distraction to lead SCP-106 away so he could

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:20.190
make it to the adjoining hallway just a few
hundred feet away.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:21.930
That was the armory.

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:25.710
Limping from his injured leg, the Plague Doctor
waited for the old man to be led away as he

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.020
made it to the room.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:31.630
He began tearing through the weaponry that
lined and leaned up against the walls in every

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:34.910
direction, ignoring the automatic rifles as
they were useless.

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:37.840
Then he found what he had been searching for.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:39.080
Flash grenades.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:42.880
As the form of another black portal began
to materialize in front of him, he pulled

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:45.900
the pin and tossed the grenade in the putrid
puddle.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:50.870
A blast of light erupted from within, followed
by the sound of the creature recoiling in

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:51.870
pain.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.310
The Plague Doctor pulled another pin.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.310
And another.

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:59.350
And in this manner he led SCP-106 toward the
secondary containment facilities that had

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.160
begun filling with fluid.

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:05.290
When he reached a level where he could recognize
the smell of kerosine, he stopped.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:10.250
There he waited, as SCP-106 emerged from the
darkness in front of him.

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:15.300
It snarled and howled, spitting black bits
of tar as it’s gnarling yellowed teeth came

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.520
close to the Plague Doctor’s face.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:21.360
The Plague Doctor calmly turned and waded
out of the half-filled room.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.500
SCP-106 tried to lunge at him, to follow.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.500
But it could not.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:30.030
It found itself rooted in liquid, unable to
easily open a portal into the space between

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.030
the walls.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:35.070
Stepping out of the room, the Plague Doctor
reached into his cloak and pulled out a large

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:37.150
match from his leather bag.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:42.290
Without glancing back he struck the match
and gave a ginger toss into the flames, sliding

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:44.270
the door closed behind him.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:49.300
The resulting explosion and subsequent inferno
damaged the walls of the secondary containment

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:53.590
facility and caused significant seismic activity
within the outer walls of the containment

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:54.590
site.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:58.980
Emergency lights flickered on and off in the
darkness and debris rained down from the ceiling

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.490
in every direction.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:04.430
In this haze of rubble, the Plague Doctor
picked himself up off the ground and began

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:08.220
to dust his cloak clean with the one hand
he had left.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:13.630
Satisfied, he took a content sigh and began
to make for the exit to the outside world,

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:18.460
where he would resume his quest to rid the
Earth of the Pestilence that plagued mankind.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:19.460
Though..

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.120
An unexpected surprise made him pause.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:28.320
A flaming corpse began to emerge from a black
hole in the wall beside him.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:35.400
SCP-106, intact and whole, the flames slowly
seeping into his skin until they were all

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:38.700
extinguished, and only smoke rose from his
body.

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:41.290
This time the doctor was not so fast to react.

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:46.200
The creature grabbed him by the face and slammed
it into a nearby wall, cracking the marble

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.200
surface.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:49.720
The black substance pooled around the Plague
Doctor’s face.

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:55.450
SCP-106 opened a portal in the wall, pushing
the Doctor's head into it.

00:21:55.450 --> 00:21:59.380
The events that followed afterwards are difficult
to put together, as camera footage from the

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:05.820
facility suffered severe damage due to SCP-049’s
explosion of the secondary containment chambers.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:10.960
SCP-106 was found back inside his cell in
the containment cube, back to his dormant

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:14.510
state where he would remain for the next few
months.

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:18.740
That is..until he would feel the need to hunt
prey once again..

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:24.520
As the doors of the 40-layer steel cube closed,
the electromagnetic supports came back online,

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:27.540
and the fluid chambers repaired and refilled.

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:32.510
The committee is currently voting on whether
or not to allow SCP-106’s containment facility

00:22:32.510 --> 00:22:33.530
to be opened again.

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:38.850
For now, The world could rest once more, Dr.
Bannon could take a sigh of relief.

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:40.880
But for how long..he thought.

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:43.710
For that, there was no way to tell..

00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:50.370
Now go check out “SCP-049 - the Plague Doctor
Captured” and “SCP-106 - The Old Man Escape”

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:53.880
for more tales of your favorite anomalous
entities from SCP Explained!

